# What never belongs in the build context.
#
# Without this file `COPY frontend/ ./` pulls in the host's node_modules --
# hundreds of megabytes of platform-specific binaries, built for the developer's
# OS and copied on top of the `npm ci` the image just ran for Linux. The root
# context additionally carried .git, both virtualenvs and the previous frontend
# build, so every `docker build` uploaded them to the daemon before doing
# anything.
#
# Deny-by-default is deliberately NOT used: the Dockerfile copies named paths
# (pyproject.toml, alembic/, app/, frontend/), so an allow-list here would state
# the same list twice and drift from it.

.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# The virtualenv, and anything a local test run leaves behind.
.venv
.pytest_cache
.coverage
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Installed inside the image by `npm ci`; the host's copy is the wrong platform.
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist

# Vite's output, copied from the frontend stage instead.
app/static

# Generated intermediate, regenerated by scripts/dump_openapi.py when needed.
openapi.json
openapi-dump.db

# Documentation, specs and tooling the runtime image has no use for.
*.md
e2e
golden-set
http
tests

# The tree `e2e/` replaced. Named separately because `e2e` above does not match
# it: a working copy that ever ran the behave suite still carries its virtualenv
# and its JUnit reports, and the build context was uploading both to the daemon
# again. `clean.sh --all` deletes the tree; this keeps it out of the image build
# until somebody does.
e2e-test-app
